# gui_lvgl app Kconfig.  An application Kconfig must source the rest of Zephyr's.

config GUI_LVGL_BENCHMARK
	bool "Run an LVGL render micro-benchmark at boot"
	default n
	help
	  Before starting the interactive UI, time per-operation render+flush
	  (fill / alpha-blend / rounded / shadow / text / gradient) over the full
	  640x480 screen and print ms-per-frame to the console.  Guides which
	  operations are worth hardware acceleration.  Needs no VNC client (it
	  renders straight into the framebuffer via the display driver).

config GUI_LVGL_BLIT_SELFTEST
	bool "Run the blitter self-test at boot"
	default n
	help
	  Before the UI/benchmark, run a standalone blitter self-test (FILL + COPY
	  of known patterns between two DDR buffers, read back by the CPU) and print
	  PASS/FAIL + first mismatches.  No LVGL/VNC involved, so it isolates the
	  blitter hardware.  Used to diagnose the DDR-retiming COPY corruption
	  (see docs/blitter-ddr-corruption-handoff.md).

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
